# What `func azure functionapp publish` must not put in the payload.
#
# The deployment package is built from this directory in place -- `wheels/` is
# written here by `make ops-package` and is the one generated thing that has to
# stay -- so this file's job is to keep the incidental out: a local settings
# file that would shadow the app's real configuration, and the caches a test run
# leaves behind.
#
# `local.settings.json` is the important line. It is where a developer would put
# a Snowflake key to run the host locally, it is in `.gitignore` for that reason,
# and a publish that uploaded it would put credentials on the app as plain
# application settings alongside the Key Vault references that exist so that
# they are not.
local.settings.json
.git*
tests
.venv
__pycache__
*.pyc
.python_packages
